course: dictionary
lesson: 9720
title: Summon: call, order or gather
level: primary-5
stars: 2
explain: Summon is a verb, and it means to call someone or something to come, often with authority. Its forms are summon, summons, summoned and summoning. Read the words around it: «The Mole hardly dares to look up — but the call and the summons still seem to command him, so he raises his eyes.» The words command and raises show that a summons is a strong call that pulls you to answer.
explain: One word can have several meanings, so check the sentence. A pupil can be «summoned to the head teacher's office», which means ordered to come. When someone is hurt, you «summon help», which means call for help. Ask yourself what would fit: in these sentences, call, order or fetch makes sense.
explain: Sometimes the call comes from inside you. «She had to summon up courage before she spoke» means she gathered her courage together to face something scary. In stories, a wizard can summon a dragon, which means call it up by magic. The clue is always in the words around it.
fact: Summon means to officially order someone to come, to call for help, to gather a feeling inside you, or to call up a creature by magic.
fact: A summons (noun) is an official order to come, such as a summons to court.
fact: Useful phrases: summon up courage, summon help, be summoned to.
fact: «The Mole hardly dares to look up — but the call and the summons still seem to command him, so he raises his eyes.» Here a summons is a strong call he feels he must obey.
fact: «People... have only the word "smell" for all the "delicate thrills which murmur in the nose of the animal night and day, summoning, warning, inciting, repelling".» Here summoning means calling something forward, the way a smell calls a feeling to mind.
exercise: «The Mole hardly dares to look up — but the call and the summons still seem to command him.» What does summons mean here? | *A strong call that seems to order him | A soft, sleepy sound | A type of cake | A happy song
exercise: Ella's teacher says, «Summon help if the lift gets stuck.» What should Ella do? | Sit down and wait quietly | Ask for a snack | Climb out through the roof | *Call for help
exercise: Nadia says, «I need to summon up courage before I sing.» What does summon up courage mean? | Lose all your courage | Buy new courage in a shop | Sing very loudly to the crowd | *Gather up courage inside yourself
test: Pupils can be «summoned to» the head teacher's office. What does summoned mean? | *Ordered to come | Kept waiting outside | Told to go to sleep | Given a prize
test: In a story, a wizard tries to summon a dragon. What does summon mean? | *Call up by magic | Paint a picture of | Hide from | Wash away
exam: Which phrase means to gather up courage inside you before a hard task? | *Summon up courage | Summon help | Be summoned to | Summoning warnings
